## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to combine a circular buffer with a monotonic deque to support rolling-window stats efficiently; checks edge-cases with duplicates and partial windows.

## Key Concepts

- Circular buffers
- Monotonic deque for max
- Running sum
- Amortized analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
class RollingWindow {
  constructor(n) {
    this.n = n;
    this.buf = new Array(n);
    this.head = 0; // points to oldest element
    this.size = 0;
    this.sum = 0;
    this.maxDQ = []; // decreasing values
  }
  push(v) {
    // evict oldest if full
    if (this.size === this.n) {
      const old = this.buf[this.head];
      this.sum -= old;
      if (this.maxDQ[0] === old) this.maxDQ.shift();
      this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.n;
      this.size--;
    }
    const idx = (this.head + this.size) % this.n;
    this.buf[idx] = v;
    this.size++;
    this.sum += v;
    while (this.maxDQ.length && this.maxDQ[this.maxDQ.length - 1] < v) this.maxDQ.pop();
    this.maxDQ.push(v);
  }
  sumWindow() {
    return this.sum;
  }
  maxWindow() {
    return this.maxDQ.length ? this.maxDQ[0] : undefined;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt to a dynamic N resize while preserving amortized guarantees?
- How does the implementation behave with all equal values or negative numbers?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests dynamic graph data structures with parallel edges and per-node statistics, a realistic scenario in routing or network monitoring.

## Key Concepts

- per-node multiset keyed by (weight, edge_id)
- order-statistic tree for kth largest
- two-endpoint synchronization on add/erase/update
- sum maintenance for O(1) incident sum reads

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor() { this.edges = new Treap(); this.sum = 0; }
  add(weight, id) { this.edges.insert(weight, id); this.sum += weight; }
  remove(weight, id) { this.edges.erase(weight, id); this.sum -= weight; }
  kthLargest(k) { return this.edges.kthLargest(k); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to handle memory pressure with millions of edges?
- How would you extend to directed graphs with asymmetric weights?

